plan.md
# Agent working plans (§2.5). Scratch, never repo content — and an
# untracked directory here is exactly what `git add -A` swept into commits.
.plans/

# Agent-runtime droppings. The daemon runs agents inside each git worktree, and
# they write their own scratch there: `cli.json`/`cursor/cli.json` are
# cursor-agent permission configs (they grant `Shell(**)` and `Shell(rm*)`), and
# `.tmp-run-*.sh`/`.run-tests.sh` are generated runners that hardcode a
# container worktree UUID and `rm -rf node_modules`. A worker's `git add -A`
# swept all of them into commits — #598 landed `cli.json` and `cursor/cli.json`
# on main, #600 carried a third copy, and none of them belong in a checkout.
cli.json
cursor/
# Generated runners and scratch the agent leaves in its worktree. Named
# individually rather than by one broad glob so an intentional dotfile is not
# swallowed: observed so far are .run-tests.sh, .tmp-run-dod-tests.sh (#600),
# and .run-targeted-tests.mjs / .test-runner-tmp.sh / .cursor-review-git-dump.py
# (#603). The shape is always "a script the agent wrote to run its own tests".
.run-*.sh
.run-*.mjs
.run-*.js
.tmp-run-*.sh
# The dotless spelling too. Every pattern above assumed a leading dot, so
# #604 landed `tmp-run-memory-tests.sh` on main unnoticed — an eighth shape
# after the seven already listed. The agent writes both spellings.
tmp-run-*.sh
tmp-run-*.mjs
tmp-run-*.js
.test-runner-tmp.*
.cursor-review-*
